  "body": "#### Root cause\n\nIn `deposit()`, the contract **locks** the deposited HYBR into the veNFT **before** computing how many gHYBR shares to mint. That makes `totalAssets()` larger by `amount` (or nearly so) when `calculateShares(amount)` is called, which **inflates the denominator** and **mints fewer shares** than fair value for the depositor.\n\nProblematic sequence (snippets with error markers):\n\n```solidity\nfunction deposit(uint256 amount, address recipient) external nonReentrant {\n    ...\n    IERC20(HYBR).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n\n    if (veTokenId == 0) {\n        _initializeVeNFT(amount);\n    } else {\n        IERC20(HYBR).approve(votingEscrow, amount);\n        IVotingEscrow(votingEscrow).deposit_for(veTokenId, amount); // <@ increases totalAssets() before share calc @>\n        _extendLockToMax();\n    }\n\n    // Calculate shares to mint based on current totalAssets\n    uint256 shares = calculateShares(amount); // <@ uses already-increased totalAssets() @>\n    _mint(recipient, shares);\n    _addTransferLock(recipient, shares);\n    ...\n}\n```\n\n`calculateShares` pulls the denominator from `totalAssets()`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction calculateShares(uint256 amount) public view returns (uint256) {\n    uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply();\n    uint256 _totalAssets = totalAssets(); // <@ denominator includes the just-deposited amount @>\n    if (_totalSupply == 0 || _totalAssets == 0) {\n        return amount;\n    }\n    return (amount * _totalSupply) / _totalAssets;\n}\n```\n\nAnd `totalAssets()` returns the veNFT’s locked amount:\n\n```solidity\nfunction totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) {\n    if (veTokenId == 0) return 0;\n    IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance memory locked =\n        IVotingEscrow(votingEscrow).locked(veTokenId);\n    return uint256(int256(locked.amount));\n}\n```\n---\n\n### **Impact**\n\nWhenever `veTokenId != 0`, every new depositor receives **fewer gHYBR shares than fair value**, because their deposit increases `totalAssets()` **before** the share calculation.\n\nThis creates a **systematic and deterministic value leak**:\n\n* **Depositors lose claim value:** Each deposit mints fewer shares than the previewed amount (via `calculateShares()`), so new participants receive a smaller proportional stake in the vault.\n* **Existing holders are over-rewarded:** The shortfall in minted shares artificially increases the share value of incumbents, effectively redistributing future rewards to them.\n\n> **Note:** The very first depositor (`_totalSupply == 0`) receives the correct 1:1 mint.\n> Every subsequent depositor is under-minted proportionally to vault growth.\n\n---\n\n### **Example — Predictable Share Mismatch**\n\n| Metric        | Before Bob’s Deposit | After Bob’s Deposit      |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `totalAssets` | 100                  | 200 (includes Bob’s 100) |\n| `totalSupply` | 100                  | —                        |\n| `deposit`     | 100                  | —                        |\n\n**Expected (if `calculateShares` called before deposit):**\n`shares = 100 * 100 / 100 = 100`\n\n**Actual (with bug, since `totalAssets` already includes deposit):**\n`shares = 100 * 100 / 200 = 50`\n\n**Result:**\nBob receives **50 gHYBR** instead of **100**, losing half of his rightful share.\nThe missing value silently accrues to existing holders, doubling their per-share entitlement.\n\nThis is a **deterministic mismatch** between the preview (`calculateShares`) and actual mint outcome — no race, randomness, or off-chain dependency. Any depositor after the first one will face a consistent under-mint proportional to total vault size.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {C4PoCTestbed} from \"./C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\n\ncontract C4PoC is C4PoCTestbed {\n    address internal alice = address(0xA11CE);\n    address internal bob = address(0xB0B);\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        // fund Alice & Bob with HYBR from deployer (deployer received initial mint in setup_InitMinter)\n        uint256 fund = 200e18;\n        vm.prank(deployer);\n        hybr.transfer(alice, fund);\n        vm.prank(deployer);\n        hybr.transfer(bob, fund);\n\n        // approvals for gHYBR to pull HYBR\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        hybr.approve(address(gHybr), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.startPrank(bob);\n        hybr.approve(address(gHybr), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    /// @notice Demonstrates that the second depositor is under-minted due to using totalAssets AFTER deposit\n    function test_DepositMintsTooFewShares_bugPoC() external {\n        // --- Alice deposits 100 HYBR ---\n        uint256 amountA = 100e18;\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        gHybr.deposit(amountA, alice);\n\n        // sanity: after first deposit, 1:1\n        assertEq(gHybr.totalAssets(), amountA, \"assets after Alice\");\n        assertEq(gHybr.totalSupply(), amountA, \"supply after Alice\");\n        assertEq(gHybr.balanceOf(alice), amountA, \"Alice shares\");\n\n        // --- Bob deposits 100 HYBR ---\n        uint256 amountB = 100e18;\n\n        // pre-deposit values *before* Bob’s deposit (the correct denominator)\n        uint256 tsBefore = gHybr.totalSupply(); // 100e18\n        uint256 taBefore = gHybr.totalAssets(); // 100e18\n\n        // Correct shares if calculated against pre-deposit assets:\n        // expectedCorrect = amountB * tsBefore / taBefore = 100 * 100 / 100 = 100\n        uint256 expectedCorrect = gHybr.calculateShares(amountB);\n\n        // What the current code effectively mints (WRONG), because it deposits first:\n        // expectedWrong = amountB * tsBefore / (taBefore + amountB) = 100 * 100 / 200 = 50\n        uint256 expectedWrong = (amountB * tsBefore) / (taBefore + amountB);\n\n        // Bob deposits\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        gHybr.deposit(amountB, bob);\n\n        uint256 actualBobShares = gHybr.balanceOf(bob);\n\n        // Show the bug: actual minted == wrong calculation; and != correct calculation\n        assertEq(\n            actualBobShares,\n            expectedWrong,\n            \"BUG: minted shares match wrong formula (under-minted)\"\n        );\n        assertTrue(\n            actualBobShares != expectedCorrect,\n            \"BUG: minted shares should have matched correct formula\"\n        );\n\n        // Extra sanity: vault doubled assets but supply only increased by 50\n        assertEq(gHybr.totalAssets(), amountA + amountB, \"assets after Bob\");\n        assertEq(\n            gHybr.totalSupply(),\n            amountA + expectedWrong,\n            \"supply after Bob\"\n        );\n    }\n\n    /// @notice This is how the mint should behave after a fix:\n    /// Move `calculateShares` BEFORE locking the HYBR, or pass `totalAssetsBefore` to the formula.\n    /// This test will currently FAIL (demonstrates intended/correct behavior).\n    function test_DepositShouldMintProportionalShares_expectedBehavior()\n        external\n    {\n        // Alice deposits 100, establishing 1:1\n        uint256 amountA = 100e18;\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        gHybr.deposit(amountA, alice);\n\n        // Bob deposits 100; we EXPECT 100 shares (1:1), which will FAIL with current bug\n        uint256 amountB = 100e18;\n        uint256 tsBefore = gHybr.totalSupply(); // 100\n        uint256 taBefore = gHybr.totalAssets(); // 100\n        uint256 expectedCorrect = gHybr.calculateShares(amountB); // 100\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        gHybr.deposit(amountB, bob);\n\n        // This assert demonstrates what the correct behavior should be.\n        // It will fail until the bug is fixed.\n        assertEq(\n            gHybr.balanceOf(bob),\n            expectedCorrect,\n            \"Should mint proportional shares against pre-deposit assets\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n```",
